Step-by-step instructions
Download and install VirtualBox
Visit the official VirtualBox website and download the installer for your operating system (Windows, macOS, or Linux). Run the installer with default settings. 
Download Ubuntu ISO
Go to the official Ubuntu website and download the latest long-term support (LTS) version of the desktop ISO for 64-bit systems.
Create a new virtual machine
Open VirtualBox, click New, and enter:
Name: Ubuntu-GitHub-VM
Type: Linux
Version: Ubuntu (64-bit)
Allocate memory (RAM)
Assign at least 4096 MB (4 GB) of RAM. Adjust based on your host system’s available memory. 
Create a virtual hard disk
Choose Create a virtual hard disk now → VDI (VirtualBox Disk Image) → Dynamically allocated → Set size to 30 GB. 
Mount the Ubuntu ISO
Select the new VM, click Settings → Storage → Empty under Controller: IDE → Click the CD icon → Choose a disk file → Select your downloaded Ubuntu ISO. 
Start the VM and install Ubuntu
Click Start. The VM will boot from the ISO. Follow the installer:
Select language
Choose Erase disk and install Ubuntu
Set username and password
Complete installation and reboot (remove ISO when prompted) 
Install Guest Additions (for better performance)
After booting into Ubuntu:
In VirtualBox menu, go to Devices → Insert Guest Additions CD Image
Open terminal in Ubuntu and run:
sudo apt update && sudo apt install build-essential dkms linux-headers-generic -y
sudo /media/$USER/VBox_GAs_*/VBoxLinuxAdditions.run

Reboot the VM.
Install Git
Open terminal and run:
sudo apt install git -y

Configure Git with GitHub
Set your GitHub credentials:
git config --global user.name "YourGitHubUsername"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"

Set up SSH for GitHub
Generate an SSH key:
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your-email@example.com"

Start the SSH agent and add your key:
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

Copy the public key:
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

Go to GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys, click New SSH key, paste the key, and save. 
Clone a GitHub repository
Test the connection:
ssh -T git@github.com

Clone your repo:
git clone git@github.com:username/your-repo.git

Optional: Enable GitHub CLI
Install GitHub CLI:
sudo apt install gh -y
gh auth login
